.! --------------------------------
.!
.newsect Method Selector Definitions
Below are listed the methods in the ${shname} system.
There abstract functionallity and return types are detailed.
Each class is free to interpret them within some leway;
after all this is an ${oo} system with data-hiding!

  The name in square brackets (_[,_]) after the method protype
is the category where the method is first defined.
Generally speaking, any method in this category of classes
or inheriting from a class in this category can respond sucessfully
to this message.

.!
.sect 1 1 Factory Methods
These methods are known by factory objects.
.!
.listum
.!
.odentry initialize [Foundation]
Perform any presetting for this class.
Returing nil will cause the application to abort.
Called before user's application begins to run.
Classes
with complex instance variable declarations that can't be encoded
during translation may change their text encoding.
.sp
A handler for cleanup may be installed by calling __oc__atExit().
The single parameter is a function that will be called
in LIFO (stack) order when the application exits.
.!
.odentry new [Foundation]
Allocate and initialize a new instance of the ${recr} class.
In contrast to [Cox86], in a factory method, it's illegal to
assign the result to the variable `self', as that refers to
the class object, and not the instance object!
.opencode
+ new
{
   id newObj;

   /*  Never assign to "self" in a factory!  */
   newObj = [super new];
   newObj->capacity = 0;
   return( newObj );
}
.endcode
.!
.odentry (int)ndxVarSize [Foundation]
Reply the count of bytes each indexed variable occupies. For non-indexing
class, the default from Object will return 0.
Effectively returns:  sizeof( [self ndxVarType] ).
.!
.odentry (STR)ndxVarType [Foundation]
Reply a string encoding that describes the instance variables that
are index-able.  For instance,
.class ByteArray,
returns "c", char type.
.!
.odentry poseAs:(classId) [Foundation]
Perform surgery and change the class of the ${recr} to a new class.
(Still under construction.)
.!
.odentry with:(int)nArgs vaDcl:(id)argList [Foundation]
Create a "sized" object, capable of holding 'nArgs' things.
Of course, the class is free is adjust to account for memory management,
and additional memory could be used by a class's superclass.
The "vaDcl:" selector is inserted automatically by the translator
when it sees a comma inside a message expression.
.!
.restore
.!
.! ---------------------
.!

.sect 1 2 Instance Methods
These methods are known by instance objects.
.listum
.!
.odentry add:item [Array and Collection]
Store 'item' at the next available slot.
If there is a notion of a cursor in self, then 'item' will be after
the cursored slot.
Array's generally store in the first unused (nil) slot.
.!
.odentry at:(int)index_ put:(id)anObject [Foundation]
Store an object into the indexing storage ${recr} object.
.!
.odentry (int) count [Array and Collection]
Return the count of usable objects contained within the object.
For Array types, 'nil' pointers are not counted.
(Was named 'size'.)
.!
.odentry error:(STR)fmtSTR vaDcl:stuff [Foundation]
Display an error message about self.
Feeds 'stuff' to an sprintf() call.
Aborts the program and never returns.
.!
.odentry find:otherObj [Array and Collection]
Returns a member that is "==" to 'otherObj'.
Returns nil if there is no match.
.!
.odentry findMatching:otherObj [Array and Collection]
Returns a member that is isEqual: to 'otherObj'.
Returns nil if there is no match.
.!
.odentry findSTR:(STR)aString [Array and Collection]
Returns a member that is isEqual: to 'aString'.
Returns nil if there is no match.
.!
.odentry first [Sequence]
Sets the objects cursor to be the first element.
Returns the first element within the list.
This is how sequencing starts.
Performing [list next] returns the second element.
.!
.odentry free [Foundation]
Releases memory used by object and returns nil.
The object is no longer usable, and any references the appliation
holds must be forgotten.
Because there is no reference counting,
free'ing an object that has an infrastructure (like
.class Set)
will create unreachable objects.
.!
.odentry freeContents [Foundation]
Walks through internal contents and frees any major sub-objects.
The internal infrastructure is invisible to the application.
Added an object after freeContents will cause the object to
rebuild its infrastructure.
.!
.odentry hash [Foundation]
Return an integer representing a the ${recr} in hashed form.
The same hash value is returned for all objects that are YES
for "isEqual:".
Ie, [obj1 hash] == [obj2 hash], iff [obj1 isSame:obj2] == YES.
Implemented in
.class Object,
so everything hash a hash value.
Re-implemented in classes like
.class ByteArray.
.!
.odentry last [Collection]
Moves a cursor to the last element stored and returns that element.
.!
.odentry toFirst [Collection]
Set a cursor inside the object to point at the first element.
Returns 'self', not the first object in the list.
Performing [list next] returns the first element.
.!
.odentry toLast [Collection]
Set a cursor inside the object to point just past the last object.
Returns 'self', not the last object in the list.
Performing [list prev] returns the last element.
.!
.restore

.endsect
.!
.! ---------------------
.!
.newsect Class Heirarchy
.!
  Listed here are the categories and which classes they contain.
Each category has a superclass listed after it, except "Foundation"
which is the base for all other classes.
Class structuring is a tradeoff between time and space.
For instance, time has been gained by not subclassing the
.class ByteArray
off of
.class Array,
but rather copying the superclass's implementation code into
.class ByteArray
and making it a subclass of
.class Object.
This saves one level of dictionary searching in __msg(),
and for a these central classes, the redundancy may be worth it.
.!
.opencode
.bold
Foundation:
   Object
      Array
      ByteArray
      IdArray
.sp
.bold
Collection (Object):
   Collection
      Set
      Sequence
      Queue
      OrderedCollection
.sp
.bold
Windowing (Object):
   View
      Fixture
         ArrowFixture
         ElevatorFixture
         StretchFixture
      NullView
      MenuBar
         PullDownMenu
            TextMenu
      StdSystemView
.endcode
.br
.endsect
.!
